erdog Texians soundly defeated Santa Anna's troops in under eighteen minutes at the Battle of San Jacinto, and in doing so won the independence for which so many had died. Kilmeade brings one of the most pivotal moments in American history to life. -- adapted from jacket  aIngrambShelf ready books10aHouston, Sam,d1793-1863.10aSanta Anna, Antonio López de,d1794-1876. 0aTexasxHistoryyRevolution, 1835-1836. 0aSan Jacinto, Battle of, Tex., 1836. 0aAlamo (San Antonio, Tex.)xSiege, 1836. 0aGovernorszTexasvBiography. 0aLegislatorszUnited StatesvBiography. 0aTexasxHistoryyTo 1846. 1aTexas 1aTexaszSan Antonio. 1aTexasxHistory. 7aHISTORYzUnited Statesx19th Century. 7aUnited StatesxHistoryxState & LocalxSouthwest (AZ, NM, OK, TX) 7governors. 7aLegislators. 7aAlamo (San Antonio, Tex.), Battle of the, 1836. 7aBattle of San Jacintoc(Texas :d1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01404392 7aRevolutionc(Texas :d1835-1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01354582 7aSiege of Alamoc(San Antonio, Texas :d1836)2fast0(OCoLC)fst01910462 7aTo 18462fast 7aBiographies.08iOnline version:aKilmeade, Brian.tSam Houston and the Alamo avengers.dNew York : Sentinel, 2019z9780525540564w(DLC)  2019022818  a92bTNT  aF390 .H84 K55 2019wLCc1i50706010953454f6/2/2025g2lSTACKSmERCp$28.00rYsYtBOOKu3/19/2021xBOOK00878cam a2200277   4500001000800000003000600008005001700014008004100031040003000072020001800102020001500120035002200135050002200157049000900179100001700188245006000205260003600265300002300301590003000324650002300354650003800377650001900415650002300434994001200457999013100469u581759SIRSI20210613042801.5200817s2020    xx            000 0 eng d  aTOHbengcTOHdJCHdOCLCO  a9780062999719  a0062999710  a(OCoLC)1192354301 0aKF4772b.C67 2020  aMAIN1 aCose, Ellis.10aShort Life and Curious Death of Free Speech in America.  bHarperCollins Publishersc2020.  a208 pages.;c23 cm  aIngrambShelf ready books 0aPolit